{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1298392-invisible-sun","id":1298392,"title":"Invisible Sun","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-21T13:55:17-07:00","id":1298392,"title":"Invisible Sun","content":"Has anyone checked out Invisible Sun by Monte Cook games? It seems to be a magic based game which is in a pretty trippy surreal world. The artwork is great and I am still trying to figure out the rules but it seems to be a great inspiration for Mage. It seems weirder than the other games from Monte Cook which is saying a lot. I should point out that the PDF is about $100.00 USD so it seems pretty pricy for an RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T14:07:19-07:00","id":1298395,"title":"","content":"It seems pretty standard urban fantasy, with the big hook being more how you play it, rather than the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T14:17:01-07:00","id":1298396,"title":"","content":"Couldn't afford it. I'm a rpg writer, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T15:06:09-07:00","id":1298405,"title":"","content":"I had my eyes on it but yeah can't afford something that pricy. I hope it isn't too hard or complex to play and that i'll be able to get i on a sale, the promotion art is right up my alley though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T15:54:36-07:00","id":1298417,"title":"","content":"Cool. The setting sounds a lot like Kult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T16:50:20-07:00","id":1298425,"title":"","content":"$100 US for a PDF is utterly ludicrous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:10:37-07:00","id":1300482,"title":"","content":"I have it (in physical and PDF - I backed the kickstarter) and...<br /> <br /> 1. It's not urban fantasy. The starting point is you leaving this world entirely for &quot;the real world&quot; which is a quasi-medieval high-metropolitan surrealist universe of multiple dimensional layers. It's weird and hard to describe.<br /> 2. &quot;The PDF&quot; (I put it in quotes because phrasing it that way is incredibly misleading) mirrors the contents of a knee-high box of books and other materials. It's somewhere in the range of nearly half a gigabyte of content - six or seven main game books, plus card decks, maps, props, tokens, adventures, art books, etc etc.<br /> <br /> So... anyone thinking it's $100 for a single PDF is mistaken. It's a very complex package and I haven't had a chance to digest all of the content it contains because it's that huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}